A||N||7||Alan Surber||85 Fiero wiring problem, no spark...||||1||
Z||000000||Alan Surber||10-16-2000||01:25 PM||||Wondering if anyone might know of a good wiring diagram or an understandable diagnostic flow chart etc. I have replaced the ECM with an extra known good one I have, had the ignition module checked, checked primary coil, pick-up coil, spark plug wires, distributor and everything within it, all good. No spark coming from coil or spark plug wire. Kind of suspect ignition or wiring harness.||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||10-16-2000||01:28 PM||||pull out the fuses and check them. The ignition module is run off one of them but I don't remember which one.<P>You did disconnect the tach filter didn't you? That will cause no spark if it's died.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Brian84SE||10-16-2000||09:39 PM||||Here's a thought:  With the distributor cap off, have someone crank the engine over to make sure the distributor shaft is turning.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Indiana_resto_guy||10-16-2000||11:30 PM||||Check for +12 volts at pin 'B' on you coil, you may have a blown fuse link after the c-500 connector. (c-500? - its part of the engine wiring harness)||||reg||1
Z||000004||Alan Surber||10-19-2000||04:11 PM||||Thanks for the input, I wanted to laugh at the "check to see if the distributor turns" reply... seems I didn't check that, tunnel vision for many electrical problems I guess. Well, it isn't turning... checked the distributor gears, they're fine.  The motor has 215,000 miles, guess it's time for an overhaul or can someone tell me how hard it is to change the cam gear or at least tell if that is stripped?||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||10-19-2000||05:19 PM||||If the distributor gear's pin is good then the only thing else is the cam gear. Make sure the dist gear pin is good. It can look OK and still be broken letting the gear turn on the shaft.<P>The gear can be replaced with the engine in the car. It's not fun but can be done. There's a few threads about that.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Carrolles||10-19-2000||05:25 PM||||Is this a 4 cyl or a v-6?<P>The v-6 uses a chain to drive the cam.<P>If you are wondering if the cam is turning have someone crank the engine while you look at the rocker arm through the oil fill hole.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Alan Surber||10-19-2000||06:51 PM||||I'm sure that the distributor teeth are good, it's a 4 cyl...||||reg||1
